  "id": "BIT-kyverno-2026-122309",
  "summary": "Kyverno before 1.19.2 Denial of Service via Unbounded CEL Policy Evaluation Cost",
  "details": "Kyverno before 1.19.2 contains a denial of service vulnerability that allows namespace-scoped policy authors to exhaust CPU and memory by submitting CEL expressions evaluated without runtime cost limits. Attackers can create a NamespacedValidatingPolicy or NamespacedDeletingPolicy with nested map comprehensions over large ConfigMap fields to OOM-kill Kyverno pods and block cluster-wide admission.",
